{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' __issue_context__.json && printf '\\\\n--- git ---\\\\n' && git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"body\": \"**CL term:**\\n- [CL_0002423](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0002423) — DN2a thymocyte\\n- [CL_0002424](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0002424) — DN2b thymocyte\\n\\nFor both DN2a and DN2b:\\n[x] in taxon: Mus musculus\\n[ ] never in taxon\\n[ ] present in taxon\\n\\n**Rationale**\\nDN2a and DN2b are defined based on c-Kit (CD117) expression levels (Kit-high vs Kit-low), following the classical DN1–DN4 (CD44/CD25) staging system. This staging system is validated only in mouse thymopoiesis.\\nHuman thymocyte development does not utilize DN2a or DN2b nomenclature, and Kit-high/Kit-low DN2 subsets are not reproducibly defined in human thymus. The Cell Ontology comment for DN2a explicitly states: “Observed in mice… molecular markers characterizing double negative thymocytes are different across species.”\\nTherefore, these terms should receive an explicit “in taxon: Mus musculus” constraint. The absence of a taxon annotation (and the presence of human_subset tags) is currently misleading.\\n\\n**References:**\\nPMID: 25060579 — Review of mouse DN1–DN4 staging; DN2a/DN2b defined via Kit-high/Kit-low only in mouse.\\nPMID: 20543111 — Experimental definition of DN2a (Kit-high) and DN2b (Kit-low) in adult mouse thymus.\\nPMID: 32079746 — Human thymus single-cell atlas; DN2a/DN2b subsets not observed or defined in human development.\",\n  \"comments\": [],\n  \"title\": \"[Taxon constraint] Add taxon constraints to DN2a (CL_0002423) and DN2b (CL_0002424)\",\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3500\"\n}\n\n--- git ---\n D .github/copilot-instructions.md\n?? AGENTS.md\n?? __agent_config__/\n?? __agent_prompt__.md\n?? __issue_context__.json\n?? __pr_result__/\n?? obo-scripts/\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
